text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium transition-colors text-white/75 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/10\" href=\"/blog\">Blog &amp; Insights</a><a class=\"block px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium transition-colors text-white/75 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/10\" href=\"/carbon-calculator\">Carbon Calculator</a><a class=\"block px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium transition-colors text-white/75 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/10\" href=\"/afri-decarbonization\">Afri Decarbonization</a><a class=\"block px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium transition-colors text-white/75 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/10\" href=\"/advisory\">Advisory Services</a><a class=\"block px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium transition-colors text-white/75 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/10\" href=\"/news\">News</a><a class=\"block px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium transition-colors text-white/75 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/10\" href=\"/gallery\">Gallery</a><a class=\"block px-4 py-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium transition-colors text-white/75 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/10\" href=\"/mothers-memorial\">Mother's Memorial</a></div></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><a href=\"/contact\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 py-2 bg-accent hover:bg-accent/90 text-accent-foreground font-semibold text-xs sm:text-sm px-4 sm:px-6 h-9 sm:h-10 rounded-lg shadow-md\">Work With Victor</button></a><button class=\"lg:hidden text-white p-2\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-menu h-6 w-6\"><line x1=\"4\" x2=\"20\" y1=\"12\" y2=\"12\"></line><line x1=\"4\" x2=\"20\" y1=\"6\" y2=\"6\"></line><line x1=\"4\" x2=\"20\" y1=\"18\" y2=\"18\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></nav></div><div class=\"fixed top-16 lg:top-20 left-0 right-0 z-40 bg-accent text-accent-foreground flex items-center justify-center py-1.5 px-8\"><a class=\"text-xs font-semibold hover:underline flex-1 text-center\" href=\"/linkedin-banner\">View Dr. Udo's Profile &amp; Banner Summary →</a><button class=\"absolute right-3 text-accent-foreground/70 hover:text-accent-foreground text-base leading-none\" aria-label=\"Dismiss\">×</button></div><main class=\"flex-1 pt-24 lg:pt-28 transition-all duration-300\"><div><div class=\"relative bg-primary text-white py-20 lg:py-28 overflow-hidden\"><div class=\"absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><div class=\"absolute -top-32 -right-32 w-96 h-96 rounded-full bg-white/[0.03]\"></div><div class=\"absolute -bottom-20 -left-20 w-64 h-64 rounded-full bg-accent/[0.07]\"></div></div><div class=\"relative max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 text-center\"><h1 class=\"font-heading text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold mb-4 leading-tight\">Abasi People Forum Podcast</h1><p class=\"text-white/70 text-lg lg:text-xl max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed\">The Voice of Abasi Nation — Speaking Truth to Power, Uniting a People, Building a Future</p></div></div><section class=\"py-20 lg:py-24 bg-background\"><div class=\"max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6\"><div class=\"max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-12\"><p class=\"text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-8\">The Abasi People Forum Podcast (APFP) is the official podcast of the Abasi People Foundation and Movement. Hosted and produced by Destiny Isong, the APFP carries the message of unity and self-emancipation for the Ibibio, Annang, Efik, Oro, Ekoi, Ekid, and Obolo peoples as one Abasi Nation — towards equitable sustainable development in Nigeria and the global diaspora. Season 1: 2025–2026.</p><div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-4 justify-center\"><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/people/ABASI-People-Online/61569615891687/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow py-2 bg-accent hover:bg-accent/90 text-accent-foreground font-semibold px-8 h-12 rounded-lg\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-facebook mr-2 h-4 w-4\"><path d=\"M18 2h-3a5 5 0 0 0-5 5v3H7v4h3v8h4v-8h3l1-4h-4V7a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h3z\"></path></svg> Listen on Facebook</button></a><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/25986634774284204/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 border bg-transparent shadow-sm py-2 border-primary text-primary hover:bg-primary hover:text-primary-foreground font-semibold px-8 h-12 rounded-lg\">Join the APF Community</button></a></div></div></div></section><section class=\"py-20 lg:py-24 bg-secondary\"><div class=\"max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6\"><div class=\"text-center mb-12 lg:mb-16\" style=\"opacity: 0;\"><span class=\"eyebrow  mb-3 block\" style=\"opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px);\">About</span><h2 class=\"font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[42px] font-bold leading-tight text-foreground\" style=\"opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px);\">About the Podcast</h2></div><div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\"><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-7 shadow-sm border border-border/50\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-3\">Host &amp; Producer</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Destiny Isong is the Host and Producer of the Abasi People Forum Podcast — giving authentic voice to the issues, aspirations, and collective vision of the Abasi Nation across Nigeria and the global diaspora.</p></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-7 shadow-sm border border-border/50\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-3\">Who We Speak For</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">The seven peoples of Abasi Nationality — Ibibio, Annang, Efik, Oro, Ekoi, Ekid, and Obolo — the fourth largest ethnic nationality in Nigeria, united under one identity: Ndito Abasi.</p></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-7 shadow-sm border border-border/50\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-3\">Our Message</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Self-emancipation of the Abasi Nation from both internal and external marginalization and exploitation, towards equitable sustainable development where no one is left behind.</p></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-7 shadow-sm border border-border/50\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-3\">Programming Format</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Routine Issue-Centric Episodes. Each episode is anchored on a specific issue facing the Abasi Nation — governance, identity, development, culture, unity, youth, or diaspora — with direct, honest, community-driven dialogue.</p></div></div></div></section><section class=\"py-20 lg:py-24 bg-background\"><div class=\"max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6\"><div class=\"text-center mb-12 lg:mb-16\" style=\"opacity: 0;\"><span class=\"eyebrow  mb-3 block\" style=\"opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px);\">Listen</span><h2 class=\"font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[42px] font-bold leading-tight text-foreground\" style=\"opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px);\">Where to Listen</h2><p class=\"mt-4 text-base lg:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mx-auto text-muted-foreground\" style=\"opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px);\">The APFP is available free on the following platforms.</p></div><div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-8\"><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-7 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-3\">Facebook (Primary)</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-6 flex-1\">All episodes live and archived on the ABASI People Online Facebook page (15,000+ followers).</p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/people/ABASI-People-Online/61569615891687/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow h-9 px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg\">Watch &amp; Listen</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-7 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-3\">TikTok</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-6 flex-1\">Episodes 20–28 available on Ibom Express TV (Reloaded) on TikTok.</p><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@ibom_express_tv2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow h-9 px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg\">Watch on TikTok</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-7 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-3\">Anchor / Spotify for Podcasters</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-6 flex-1\">Hosted on Anchor with distribution to major platforms. Subscribe free.</p><a href=\"https://anchor.fm/sustainability-leadership\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow h-9 px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg\">Listen on Anchor</button></a></div></div><div class=\"bg-secondary rounded-lg p-5 text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto\"><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">For partnerships, distribution inquiries, or to suggest episode topics, contact <span class=\"font-semibold\">info@victorudo.com</span>.</p></div></div></section><section class=\"py-20 lg:py-24 bg-secondary\"><div class=\"max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6\"><div class=\"text-center mb-12 lg:mb-16\" style=\"opacity: 0;\"><span class=\"eyebrow  mb-3 block\" style=\"opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px);\">Episodes</span><h2 class=\"font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[42px] font-bold leading-tight text-foreground\" style=\"opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px);\">Episodes — Season 1 (2025–2026)</h2><p class=\"mt-4 text-base lg:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mx-auto text-muted-foreground\" style=\"opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px);\">28 episodes of direct, issue-centric dialogue on emancipation, governance, unity, and equitable development for Ndito Abasi.</p></div><div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-3 justify-center mb-8\"><button class=\"px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium transition-all bg-primary text-primary-foreground\">All</button><button class=\"px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium transition-all bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground hover:bg-secondary/80\">Governance</button><button class=\"px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium transition-all bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground hover:bg-secondary/80\">Emancipation &amp; Identity</button><button class=\"px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium transition-all bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground hover:bg-secondary/80\">Development</button><button class=\"px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium transition-all bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground hover:bg-secondary/80\">Unity</button><button class=\"px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium transition-all bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground hover:bg-secondary/80\">Culture</button><button class=\"px-4 py-2 rounded-full text-sm font-medium transition-all bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground hover:bg-secondary/80\">Youth</button></div><div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\"><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">1.</span> Introduction to the Abasi People Forum Podcast</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">July 28, 2025</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Emancipation &amp; Identity</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">The inaugural episode of the APFP — introducing the podcast, its mission, and the Abasi Nation movement for unity and equitable development.</p><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow hover:bg-primary/90 px-4 py-2 w-full bg-muted text-muted-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10 cursor-not-allowed opacity-60\" disabled=\"\">Coming to Archive</button></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">2.</span> Who Are the Abasi People?</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">August 4, 2025</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Emancipation &amp; Identity</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">A foundational episode establishing the identity, history, and shared heritage of the seven peoples of Abasi Nationality.</p><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow hover:bg-primary/90 px-4 py-2 w-full bg-muted text-muted-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10 cursor-not-allowed opacity-60\" disabled=\"\">Coming to Archive</button></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">3.</span> Abasi — The Divine Thread of Unity</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">August 11, 2025</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Unity</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">\"Abasi is the divine thread that weaves Ibibio, Annang, Efik, Oro, Ekid, Obolo, and Ekoi people into one nationality fabric with a shared identity and culture.\" — Dr. Victor Udo</p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1LcAQuzj1E/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">4.</span> The Case for Abasi Nation Self-Governance</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">August 18, 2025</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Governance</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">Examining the structural and political case for greater Abasi Nation self-governance within the Nigerian federal system.</p><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow hover:bg-primary/90 px-4 py-2 w-full bg-muted text-muted-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10 cursor-not-allowed opacity-60\" disabled=\"\">Coming to Archive</button></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">5.</span> Marginalization and the Path Forward</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">August 25, 2025</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Emancipation &amp; Identity</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">A candid conversation on the internal and external forces of marginalization facing the Abasi Nation and the roadmap to collective emancipation.</p><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow hover:bg-primary/90 px-4 py-2 w-full bg-muted text-muted-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10 cursor-not-allowed opacity-60\" disabled=\"\">Coming to Archive</button></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">6.</span> Shared Identity as the Foundation for Equitable Development</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">September 2025</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Emancipation &amp; Identity</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">Why a unified Abasi identity is the non-negotiable foundation for achieving equitable and sustainable development for all Ndito Abasi.</p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/share/r/1e15jZVwSm/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">7.</span> Self-Control and Resource Management — The Path to Autonomy</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">September 21, 2025</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Governance</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">\"We are not advocating for any form of disintegration in Nigeria. Instead, we emphasize the need for greater self-control and more effective management of human and natural resources to achieve equitable and sustainable development across Abasi Nation.\" — Dr. Victor Udo</p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1GUHTEZfZF/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">8.</span> Building the Abasi People Foundation — Vision and Structure</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">September 2025</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Emancipation &amp; Identity</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">An inside look at the founding, structure, and strategic vision of the Abasi People Foundation and its role in uniting Ndito Abasi globally.</p><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow hover:bg-primary/90 px-4 py-2 w-full bg-muted text-muted-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10 cursor-not-allowed opacity-60\" disabled=\"\">Coming to Archive</button></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">9.</span> Growing the Abasi Nation Movement</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">October 18, 2025</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Unity</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">A progress update on the Abasi People Foundation movement — its reach, growing membership, and the momentum building across Nigeria and the diaspora.</p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1Cu96GWN1S/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">10.</span> APF Momentum — A New Season of Mobilization</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">October 27, 2025</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Unity</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">Reflecting on a pivotal moment in the APF's growth and calling on all Ndito Abasi to join the movement for collective emancipation.</p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/share/v/17eDFiZ7pK/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">11.</span> Raising World-Class Talent from Abasi Nation</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">November 2, 2025</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Youth</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">How do we produce global superstars — in music, business, sport, and leadership — from Ibibio, Annang, Efik, Oro, Ekid, Obolo, and Ekoi? What must we do differently to develop and celebrate our own?</p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1B6iHrBSem/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors fo