fy-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">22.</span> Abasi Nation — Season 1 Episode 22</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">February 2026</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Governance</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">Direct, honest dialogue on governance and representation for the Abasi Nation.</p><a href=\"https://vm.tiktok.com/ZNRX259kH/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">23.</span> Abasi Nation — Season 1 Episode 23</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">February 2026</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Development</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">Pathways to equitable development across all seven Abasi communities.</p><a href=\"https://vm.tiktok.com/ZNRX2Y2KM/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">24.</span> Abasi Nation — Season 1 Episode 24</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">March 2026</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Emancipation &amp; Identity</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">The ongoing conversation on identity, self-determination, and dignity for all Ndito Abasi.</p><a href=\"https://vm.tiktok.com/ZNRX2y36o/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">25.</span> Abasi Nation — Season 1 Episode 25</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">March 2026</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Youth</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">The role of Abasi youth in leading the next generation of the emancipation movement.</p><a href=\"https://vm.tiktok.com/ZNRX2RhWu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">26.</span> Abasi Nation Cultural Heritage — Our Shared Ancestry and Collective Future</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">March 20, 2026</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Culture</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">The Abasi Nation encompasses Ibibio, Annang, Efik, Oro, Ekid, Obolo, and Ekoi — the fourth largest ethnic bloc in Nigeria. This episode explores the shared heritage, spiritual bonds, and the call on Senators Akpabio and Ekayenyi and Governors Otu and Eno to deliver equitable development as the Ibom Deep Seaport comes online.</p><a href=\"https://vm.tiktok.com/ZNRX22hMq/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">27.</span> Abasi Nation — Season 1 Episode 27</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">March 2026</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Governance</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">Continuing the call for equal representation and equitable governance for all Ndito Abasi within Nigeria's national structure.</p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/share/v/1TTy7MvVAB/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-base font-bold text-foreground leading-snug flex-1\"><span class=\"text-accent font-semibold\">28.</span> One Abasi Nation — Unity Amplifies Strength</h3></div><p class=\"text-xs text-muted-foreground mb-3\">March 27, 2026</p><span class=\"inline-block bg-accent/10 text-accent text-xs font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3 w-fit\">Emancipation &amp; Identity</span><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-5 flex-1\">The Abasi People Foundation reaffirms that the Abasi Nation — as the fourth largest ethnic nationality in Nigeria — commands significant national influence. Identifying as a unified Abasi Nation amplifies collective strength and accelerates development. Fragmentation weakens. Unity wins.</p><a href=\"https://vm.tiktok.com/ZNRX2MNMk/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow px-4 py-2 w-full bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 text-primary-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg text-sm h-10\">Watch Episode</button></a></div></div></div></section><section class=\"py-20 lg:py-24 bg-background\"><div class=\"max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6\"><div class=\"text-center mb-12 lg:mb-16\" style=\"opacity: 0;\"><span class=\"eyebrow  mb-3 block\" style=\"opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px);\">Engage</span><h2 class=\"font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[42px] font-bold leading-tight text-foreground\" style=\"opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px);\">Be Part of the Movement</h2><p class=\"mt-4 text-base lg:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mx-auto text-muted-foreground\" style=\"opacity: 0; transform: translateY(15px);\">The Abasi People Forum Podcast is more than a podcast — it is a platform for the collective voice of Ndito Abasi. Follow, share, and engage.</p></div><div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6\"><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-7 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-3\">Follow the Podcast</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-6 flex-1\">Follow ABASI People Online on Facebook to get notified when new episodes drop.</p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/people/ABASI-People-Online/61569615891687/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow h-9 px-4 py-2 w-full bg-accent hover:bg-accent/90 text-accent-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg\">Follow on Facebook</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-7 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-3\">Join the Community</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-6 flex-1\">Join the Abasi People Foundation Facebook group to engage directly with APF leadership and fellow Ndito Abasi.</p><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/25986634774284204/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow h-9 px-4 py-2 w-full bg-accent hover:bg-accent/90 text-accent-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg\">Join APF Group</button></a></div><div class=\"bg-card rounded-lg p-7 shadow-sm border border-border/50 hover:shadow-md hover:-translate-y-0.5 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-3\">Contact APF</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-6 flex-1\">To suggest episode topics, request appearances, or partner with the APFP.</p><a href=\"/contact\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><button class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 shadow h-9 px-4 py-2 w-full bg-accent hover:bg-accent/90 text-accent-foreground font-semibold rounded-lg\">Contact APF</button></a></div></div></div></section><section class=\"py-20 lg:py-24 bg-secondary\"><div class=\"max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6\"><div class=\"max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center bg-card rounded-lg p-8 shadow-sm border border-border/50\"><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">The Abasi People Forum Podcast is a production of the Abasi People Foundation. Host &amp; Producer: Destiny Isong. Founding Chairman/President/CEO: Dr. Victor Udo, PhD, FNSE. For partnership and media inquiries: <span class=\"font-semibold\">info@victorudo.com</span></p></div></div></section></div></main><footer class=\"bg-primary text-white\"><div class=\"max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 lg:py-20\"><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-10 lg:gap-8\"><div class=\"sm:col-span-2 lg:col-span-1\"><h3 class=\"font-heading text-xl font-bold mb-1\">Victor Udo, FNSE, PhD</h3><p class=\"text-white/60 text-xs leading-relaxed mb-4\"><a class=\"underline decoration-white/30 hover:text-white hover:decoration-white transition-colors\" href=\"/about\">Engineer</a> · <a class=\"underline decoration-white/30 hover:text-white hover:decoration-white transition-colors\" href=\"/about\">Executive</a> · <a class=\"underline decoration-white/30 hover:text-white hover:decoration-white transition-colors\" href=\"/veu-ai-studio\">AI Builder</a> · <a class=\"underline decoration-white/30 hover:text-white hover:decoration-white transition-colors\" href=\"/publications\">Author</a> · <a class=\"underline decoration-white/30 hover:text-white hover:decoration-white transition-colors\" href=\"/abasi-people\">Community Leader</a></p><p class=\"text-white/50 text-xs leading-relaxed\"><a class=\"underline decoration-white/30 hover:text-white hover:decoration-white transition-colors\" href=\"/veu-ai-studio\">Founder, VEU AI Studio</a> · <a class=\"underline decoration-white/30 hover:text-white hover:decoration-white transition-colors\" href=\"/afri-decarbonization\">Chairman/CEO, Afri Decarbonization Corporation</a> · <a class=\"underline decoration-white/30 hover:text-white hover:decoration-white transition-colors\" href=\"/abasi-people\">Founding Chairman/President/CEO, Abasi People Foundation</a> · <a class=\"underline decoration-white/30 hover:text-white hover:decoration-white transition-colors\" href=\"/about\">Former Director of Sustainability &amp; Chairman, President's Sustainability Council — Bucknell University (2019–2025)</a></p></div><div><h4 class=\"t